<%#
    The two store links, in one file because four pages want them and a dead
    store URL is the kind of thing you only notice from a bug report.

    The names really are different. "Weekly Budget" was already taken on the App
    Store, so the iOS app is listed as "Weekly Spend" — saying so here saves
    someone searching the wrong store for the wrong name.

    `locals.review` points the same two listings at their rating flow, for the
    About page. Read via locals, like bottomnav's `active`: a bare `review` would
    be a ReferenceError on the pages that do not set it. Apple takes a query
    parameter that opens the listing with the rating sheet already up; Play has
    no equivalent, so that one lands on the listing and the reader taps a star.
%>
<ul class="app-links">
    <li>
        <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/id6803146065<%= locals.review ? '?action=write-review' : '' %>">Weekly Spend</a>
        <%= locals.review ? 'on the App Store' : 'for iPhone and iPad' %>
    </li>
    <li>
        <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.andrewovens.weeklybudget2">Weekly Budget</a>
        <%= locals.review ? 'on Google Play' : 'for Android' %>
    </li>
</ul>
